<title>UK: Iceland up on MBO talk, sector strength.</title>
<headline>Iceland up on MBO talk, sector strength.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Iceland Group Plc continued to advance on Tuesday, buoyed by the strength of the UK food retail sector and by market talk of a possible management buy-out of the company, traders said.</p>
<p>By 1146 GMT, Iceland shares were 1-1/2p firmer at 94 on volume of a million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;There's been a bit of talk about a management buy-out which has been drawing in some speculative buyers,&quot; one dealer said. &quot;But the whole sector is very strong so we'd expect to see Iceland up.&quot;</p>
<p>Iceland's spokesman was not immediately available for comment on the management buy-out speculation.</p>
